.TH BB 1 "September 2026" "bb 0.3.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
bb \- Backbencher Brain, universal code intelligence for 40+ languages
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B bb
[\fIoptions\fR] [\fIcommand\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B bb
indexes a codebase into a local knowledge base (AST, symbols, embeddings)
and serves it to humans and AI agents: keyword and semantic search, question
answering over the index, health reporting, and an MCP server that editors
and agent hosts can connect to.
.PP
Embedding vectors make semantic search (\fIbb_search\fR, \fIbb_ask\fR) much
more precise. Without a configured embedding provider, semantic search falls
back to local word vectors, which are deliberately weaker; both kinds of
vectors are stored separately, labeled by producing model, and never compared
across vector spaces.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B tool
Run one of the public tools with JSON arguments (the MCP surface, also usable
from scripts).
.TP
.BI index " dir"
Index a project. The first interactive run offers embedding setup when no
provider is configured yet; the wizard prompts only once (an explicit skip is
remembered). Re-run with
.B \-\-force
after changing the embedding model so stored vectors are rebuilt.
.TP
.B setup
Configure the embedding provider interactively: pick a prefilled free
provider or a custom OpenAI-compatible endpoint, paste the API key (input is
hidden), the key is validated with one live /embeddings call before it is
saved, and the config is written with permissions 0600.
.TP
.B setup show
Print the effective embedding configuration: every precedence tier (env,
global, project), the winning tier, and the key as a last-four fingerprint
only. The full key is never displayed. Exits 1 when nothing is configured.
.TP
.B doctor
Diagnose embedding setup and index consistency from real local state (config
tiers, file permissions, and the models actually stored in the project
index). Every finding names the exact fix command. Read-only. Exits 1 when a
hard finding exists, for example a model mismatch between configuration and
index.
.TP
.B doctor \-\-fix
Repair config file permissions to 0600 only. This is the single mutating arm
of doctor: every change is printed, and everything else (keys, config
content, index) is never modified.
.TP
.BI search " query"
Search the index (keyword and semantic modes).
.TP
.BI health " [dir]"
Index health and freshness.
.TP
.BI onboard " [dir]"
Write the bb tools guidance section into
.I <dir>/AGENTS.md
so an agent host discovers the bb tools without being told. The section is
generated from the tool registry (it can never name a tool that does not
exist), and writing is idempotent: only the block between the
.B bb:onboard
markers is replaced, everything else in the file is preserved.
.B \-\-check
reports drift or ghost tool names and exits 1 without writing;
.B \-\-print
shows the generated section; 
.B \-\-file
chooses another guide file.
.TP
.B mcp
Start the MCP server over stdio for Claude Code, Cursor, VS Code, and other
MCP hosts.
.TP
.B version
Print the bb version (same as
.B \-v
and
.B \-\-version
).
.TP
.B help
Show help for any command.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-v ", " \-\-version
Output the version number.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Display help for the command.
.SH EMBEDDING SETUP
Configuration precedence is: environment variables
.RB ( BB_EMBEDDING_BASE_URL ,
.BR BB_EMBEDDING_API_KEY ,
.BR BB_EMBEDDING_MODEL ),
then the global config
.B ~/.bb/config.json
(written by
.BR bb\ setup ),
then the project file
.BR bb.json .
The config file holds an API key, so it is written with permissions 0600; if
it is ever more open, `bb doctor` warns and `bb doctor --fix` repairs the
permissions. Free-tier providers are offered in the wizard (OpenRouter,
NVIDIA NIM), and any OpenAI-compatible /embeddings endpoint can be used as a
custom provider. After adding or changing a model, refresh stored vectors
with `bb index --force`.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Success, or doctor found only warnings (no hard finding).
.TP
.B 1
Error, or a hard finding exists (for example: nothing configured, or the
index was built with a different embedding model than the configuration).
.SH SEE ALSO
The repository README and EMBEDDINGS.md document setup, diagnostics, and the
honesty rules in full.
